## Everyday commands

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Install / update the CLI | `go install github.com/Xwudao/neter/cmd/nr@latest` |
| Dev with hot reload | `nr dev` |
| Run without reload | `nr run` |
| Build backend | `nr build` |
| Build backend + frontend | `nr build --web` |
| Print a full `neter.yml` example | `nr config-example` |
| Regenerate route info / TS types | `nr route-info` |
| Scaffold code | `nr gen ...` |
| Database migrations | `nr migrate ...` |
| Regenerate this skill | `nr skills` |

Run `nr <command> --help` for every flag.

## Scaffold code

`nr gen biz -n <name>` creates `internal/biz/<name>_biz.go`. Common flags:

- `--with-iface` — Biz interface plus a mockgen directive
- `--with-params` — `internal/domain/params/<name>_params.go`
- `--with-crud` — basic CRUD in the Biz and Repository (needs a model, see below)
- `--with-contracts` — HTTP-independent Command/Query contracts
- `--no-repo` — skip the repository
- `--skip-wire` — do not touch the Wire provider set

After adding providers, regenerate Wire from the package that owns them
(`cd cmd/app && wire`, `cd internal/cmd_app && wire`).

{{if .IsSQLC}}
## sqlc stack (this project)

SQL is the source of truth. Edit `db/migrations/*.sql` and `db/query/*.sql`,
then regenerate with `make sqlc` (or `sqlc generate`).

### Generate a resource

```bash
nr gen biz -n order --with-crud --model Order --plural Orders
```

This emits a `sqlc.<Model>` interface and repository stub. Then:

1. Add the matching queries to `db/query/orders.sql`, following the naming
   convention `ListOrders`, `GetOrder`, `CreateOrder`, `UpdateOrder`,
   `DeleteOrder`.
2. Run `make sqlc` to regenerate `internal/data/sqlc`.
3. Replace the `errOrderNotImplemented` placeholders in the generated
   repository with `data.Queries` calls.

`nr new`, `nr gen ent`, and `nr show ent` target the legacy Ent stack and will
refuse to run here.

### Database migrations

```bash
nr migrate new add_orders      # creates db/migrations/000NNN_add_orders.{up,down}.sql
# edit both files, then:
nr migrate up                  # apply pending migrations
nr migrate status
nr migrate down [--all] [--steps N]
nr migrate force <version>     # recover a dirty schema
```

DSN resolution: `--dsn` > `NETER_DSN` / `DATABASE_URL` > `config.yml db:`.
A deployed binary can migrate itself on startup when `db.autoMigrate: true`
(or `NETER_AUTO_MIGRATE=true`); the migrations are embedded in the binary.

`nr route-info` prints a notice for sqlc projects and is not maintained here.
{{end}}

{{if .IsEnt}}
## Legacy Ent stack (this project)

Persistence is Ent + MySQL; the schema lives in `internal/data/ent/schema`.

```bash
nr new <Name>      # create an Ent schema
nr gen ent         # go generate ./ent
nr show ent        # describe the Ent schema
```

`nr gen biz --with-crud --ent-name <Entity>` emits `ent.<Entity>` code.

`nr migrate new/up/down/status/force` only runs file-based SQL under
`db/migrations`; it does not apply Ent schema changes. Use `nr gen ent` plus
the application's own migrate command for Ent.

A sqlc project is detected by `sqlc.yaml` or `db/query/`; if either appears,
the CLI switches to the new stack.
{{end}}

## Frontend / SPA

- Source lives in `web/` (Vite).
- `nr build --web` builds it and copies `web/dist` to `assets/dist`, which is
  embedded into the Go binary.
- `web/vite.config.ts` must keep `build.manifest: true`; the SPA middleware
  reads `.vite/manifest.json`.
- A fresh clone has no built `assets/dist`. The backend still starts (it only
  logs a warning), but SPA routes 404 until the web app is built.

## Conventions

- Do not edit generated code: `internal/data/sqlc/**`, `*_gen.go`,
  `assets/dist/**`, or this `SKILL.md`.
- Mocks: `make mock`. Tests: `make test`. sqlc: `make sqlc`. Wire: `make wire`.
- Wire is generated per package; re-run it after changing providers.
